EXPERIMENT 46 – UNIT TESTING USING STUB AND DRIVER WITH JUNIT
AIM
To write JUnit test cases to design a test harness using a stub and a driver to unit test a fare calculation module.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the JUnit 5 junit-jupiter dependency.
2. Write the DistanceService interface to return the distance in kilometres between two stops.
3. Replace the real implementation with a stub.
4. Create the FareCalculator class using the formula:
   
   Fare = 50 + 12 × Distance (km)
5. Create FareCalculatorTest as the driver.
6. Create stubs using lambda expressions that return fixed distances 10, 0 and -5.
7. Verify using assertEquals() and assertThrows().
8. Run tests using mvn test.
CODE
1. DistanceService.java
public interface DistanceService {
    int getDistanceKm(String from, String to);
}


2. FareCalculator.java
public class FareCalculator {
    private static final int BASE_FARE = 50;
    private static final int RATE_PER_KM = 12;

    private final DistanceService distanceService;

    public FareCalculator(DistanceService distanceService) {
        this.distanceService = distanceService;
    }

    public int fare(String from, String to) {
        int km = distanceService.getDistanceKm(from, to);

        if (km < 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Invalid distance");
        }

        return BASE_FARE + km * RATE_PER_KM;
    }
}


3. FareCalculatorTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class FareCalculatorTest {

    @Test
    void fareForTenKm() {
        DistanceService stub = (from, to) -> 10;
        FareCalculator calculator = new FareCalculator(stub);

        assertEquals(170,
            calculator.fare("Chennai", "Tambaram"));
    }

    @Test
    void fareForZeroKm() {
        FareCalculator calculator =
            new FareCalculator((from, to) -> 0);

        assertEquals(50,
            calculator.fare("Guindy", "Guindy"));
    }

    @Test
    void invalidDistanceThrows() {
        FareCalculator calculator =
            new FareCalculator((from, to) -> -5);

        assertThrows(IllegalStateException.class,
            () -> calculator.fare("A", "B"));
    }
}


